  "finalText": "The NOVA logo reveal is built on the 4-second comp, navy background with a mint accent (`#2EE6A6`), and the lockup holds from about 2.7 s to the end.\n\n- **Mark** (**Mark ring**, **Mark slash**): the white ring draws on from 0.2 s, then the mint diagonal slash cuts across it from 0.9 s.\n- **Wordmark** (**Wordmark reveal** / **Wordmark NOVA**): \"NOVA\" starts hidden behind the mark's right edge, in a clipping group, and slides out from 1.25 to 2.15 s with a small 5% settle.\n- **Tagline** (**Tagline**): \"Money, made simple\" fades in and rises slightly from 2.0 s, under the wordmark.\n\nThe first pass had the wordmark sitting visible before its slide; I fixed that by keying it fully hidden at the start. The critic scores the piece 82/100. Its remaining notes ask for more secondary motion during the hold, which I left out so the ending stays clean as you asked. I can add a subtle accent pulse on the slash if you want the hold to breathe."
